# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere.
#
# Enforce LF in the repository AND in every checkout, on every platform.
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks out CRLF working copies,
# which fail `biome format` locally (and the husky pre-commit hook) even though
# the committed blobs are already LF and CI on Linux stays green. `text=auto`
# lets git keep auto-detected binary files untouched; the explicit `binary`
# rules below are belt-and-suspenders for assets git might otherwise sniff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize, never touch line endings.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF regardless of detection (CRLF breaks the shebang).
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Drizzle schema snapshots + journal are generated by `db:generate` and committed
# (Drizzle diffs against them to produce the next migration — see docs/db.md), but
# they're large and never read by humans. `linguist-generated` collapses them by
# default in GitHub diffs and drops them from the repo's language stats. They stay
# tracked — this only changes how they DISPLAY, not whether they're versioned.
packages/db/drizzle/meta/*.json linguist-generated
